Title: F1-M03 — The North Road (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. STAGING POST MOTOR SHED - PRE-DAWN

[[AMBIENCE: idling diesel, a hoist chain, boots on gravel]]
[[MUSIC: restrained military tension]]

A route map is pinned to a workbench between oil cans. CAPTAIN ELIAN and MIRA stand over it. RUSK leans against the doorframe, manifest in his belt.

RUSK
(tired)
Four trucks. Fuel, field radios, medical stores. The northern garrison has two days without them, and I am not counting the second day.

MIRA
(serious)
The valley road is exposed. If the trucks stop, the whole column becomes a target.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: valley road west to east, south ridge with two side valleys, river to the north, rock cut at the halfway point, forest above it, walled garrison at the east edge]]

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(firm)
Escort the convoy to the garrison. If the main road is blocked, keep the vehicles together and take the forest route.

RUSK
(economical)
Forty kilometres. One hour of fuel margin. The drivers roll when nothing is shooting within sight, and they do not roll a minute longer than that.

MIRA
(dry)
There are riflemen on the ridge above the first waypoint, and they have been there since yesterday. Watchers, not raiders. The question is what they are waiting to see.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(short)
Two tanks, six rifles, two rocket troopers. Screen the ridge, kill what comes out of the side valleys, keep the repair truck behind the lead tank.

RUSK
(irritated)
Lose two trucks and I turn the rest round. Half a convoy feeds nobody.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(neutral)
Then we lose none. Move out.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
